{"architectures":["x64"],"id":"LoftLabs.DevPod","latestVersion":"0.6.15","media":{"icons":[{"mimeType":"image/png","path":"media/icon.03dab69f.png","priority":1,"sha256":"03dab69fbac33a5395e9703770023be80c7cee94313e914d6ce95e425daef49e","source":"winget-legacy"}],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"description":"Codespaces but open-source, client-only and unopinionated: Works with any IDE and lets you use any cloud, kubernetes or just localhost docker.","license":"MPL-2.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/loft-sh/devpod/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"description":"Codespaces but open-source, client-only and unopinionated: Works with any IDE and lets you use any cloud, kubernetes or just localhost docker.","license":"MPL-2.0","licenseUrl":"https://github.com/loft-sh/devpod/blob/HEAD/LICENSE","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"DevPod is a client-only tool to create reproducible developer environments based on a devcontainer.json on any backend. Each developer environment runs in a container and is specified through a devcontainer.json. Through DevPod providers, these environments can be created on any backend, such as the local computer, a Kubernetes cluster, any reachable remote machine, or in a VM in the cloud.\nYou can think of DevPod as the glue that connects your local IDE to a machine where you want to develop. So depending on the requirements of your project, you can either create a workspace locally on the computer, on a beefy cloud machine with many GPUs, or a spare remote computer. Within DevPod, every workspace is managed the same way, which also makes it easy to switch between workspaces that might be hosted somewhere else.","moniker":"devpod","name":"DevPod","packageUrl":"https://devpod.sh/","publisher":"loft","publisherUrl":"https://www.loft.sh/","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/loft-sh/devpod/releases/tag/v0.6.15","tags":["cloud","container","devcontainer","develop","development","docker","k8s","kubernetes","remote-development","remote-development-environment","vscode"]},"zh-CN":{"description":"codespaces，但是开源、仅限客户端且无预设：可与任何 IDE 配合使用，并允许您使用任何云服务、Kubernetes 或仅本地主机上的 Docker。","locale":"zh-CN","longDescription":"DevPod 是一款纯客户端工具，可在任意后端基于 devcontainer.json 创建可复现的开发环境。每个开发环境都运行在容器中，并通过 devcontainer.json 文件进行配置。借助 DevPod 提供程序，这些环境可以创建在任何后端上，例如本地计算机、Kubernetes 集群、任何可访问的远程机器或云中的虚拟机。\n您可以将 DevPod 视为连接本地 IDE 与目标开发机器的桥梁。因此根据项目需求，您既可以在本地计算机上创建工作区，也可以在配备多块 GPU 的云端高性能机器或闲置远程计算机上创建。在 DevPod 中，所有工作区都以统一方式管理，这使得切换可能部署在不同位置的工作区变得异常便捷。","tags":["docker","k8s","kubernetes","vscode","云","容器","开发","开发容器","开发环境","远程开发","远程开发环境"]}},"longDescription":"DevPod is a client-only tool to create reproducible developer environments based on a devcontainer.json on any backend. Each developer environment runs in a container and is specified through a devcontainer.json. Through DevPod providers, these environments can be created on any backend, such as the local computer, a Kubernetes cluster, any reachable remote machine, or in a VM in the cloud.\nYou can think of DevPod as the glue that connects your local IDE to a machine where you want to develop. So depending on the requirements of your project, you can either create a workspace locally on the computer, on a beefy cloud machine with many GPUs, or a spare remote computer. Within DevPod, every workspace is managed the same way, which also makes it easy to switch between workspaces that might be hosted somewhere else.","moniker":"devpod","name":"DevPod","packageUrl":"https://devpod.sh/","publisher":"loft","publisherUrl":"https://www.loft.sh/","releaseNotesUrl":"https://github.com/loft-sh/devpod/releases/tag/v0.6.15","tags":["cloud","container","devcontainer","develop","development","docker","k8s","kubernetes","remote-development","remote-development-environment","vscode"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/0.6.15/app.json","detailSha256":"3acdca7f21108a7c98958f0d0fd9aff986c8b8355da2ce487bb7cfe5cc87d3ba",